+Each main object is one SQLite table. A record assembled from several stores
+or from files beside a Run is a defect, not a model.
+
+A Run has three nullable parents. Given an invocation whose Task is set, the
+constructor fills `task`; given a Task, it fills `wave` from the Task's
+Project. Supplying a parent that disagrees with the filled one is refused, so
+`(none, task)` and a Run whose Wave is not its Task's Wave cannot exist.
+`work_source` records how the Task or Wave was set: `declared` (`--task`,
+`--wave`, `--as`), `checkout` (the branch of the launch checkout belongs to a
+Task), `inherited` (an Ask copies its parent Run's parents), or `bound`
+(`lf session bind` after launch). Inside an invocation the Run also records
+its node and iteration tuple. Bind changes `task` and `wave`; it never changes
+the invocation, node, or tuple.
+
+A Session is a child of exactly one Run and reads its Task, Wave, provider,
+and Flow membership through that Run. It owns only what a person changes:
+`kind` (`interactive`, `flow_review`, `ask`), `title` with its provenance
+(`generated` or `human`), `state`, and `ready_summary`. Rename and bind are
+row updates; nothing is written beside the Run record.
+
+A Flow invocation is fully unrolled when created: composed sub-Flows are
+expanded into one graph, so `parent` on an invocation means runtime nesting
+only (a loop body entered on a pass), never template composition. Naming keeps
+"Flow" for the template and "Flow invocation" for the running object
+(default; open). A Task's current invocation normally unrolls its Project's
+Flow; `lf task run --flow` may invoke another, and the invocation records
+which (default; open).
+
 Run identity records causality and provenance. It never grants Work mutation,
 credential, Git, or process-signal authority.
 
